netflix bought the rights for their most  watched non-english show money heist for  just two dollars the streaming service  made an incredibly smart investment one  that allowed money heist to bring more  impressive production values than the  creators could have imagined success  didn't come without its issues though  sometimes fans swarmed the set and  halted filming while other days intense  weather either ruined the set and props  or caused the actors to nearly  over the course of the series a whopping  300 different locations were used to  film that's not all though the cast and  crew were regularly crossing borders  since they shot scenes in seven  different countries denmark thailand  panama italy portugal and the uk  the show obviously has a massive  following and some of the fans wanted to  get even closer to the action one  particularly hectic day saw 4 000 fans  show up and watch the filming silently  pedro alonso and alvaro morte decided to  thank the fans for being so wonderful  but with 4 000 people wanting to say  hello filming wound up having to be  halted  [Music]  filming this scene that's meant to take  place in the chilly north atlantic  oceans was actually shot in thailand  under extreme heat conditions up to 44  degrees the actors seriously struggled  alvaro morte had to be fanned by crew  members on set to prevent him from  fainting and controlling the amount of  sweat coming through his clothing at  least when the actors were rehearsing  they were able to strip down and work  somewhat comfortably  things got a little too real for the  arturo actor when he was being treated  after being shot in the chest the team  decided they wanted the actor to undergo  actual stitches so a real surgeon was  brought to the set to perform the task  for the cameras cast and crew the cast  was very squirmy watching and were  fighting laughter throughout the scene  because of how crazy the whole situation  was  the original budget for the show was  pretty minimal compared to the later  seasons while they did eventually end up  filming around the world the team didn't  leave spain for the first two seasons  once netflix invested the whole  production got major upgrades including  access to expensive features like  private islands remarkable buildings and  helicopters cast knew they were really  gaining success when their social media  following jumped into the thousands  netflix definitely made a good  investment they didn't do any  advertising and had minimal costs to add  translations and do some restructuring  on the show  the money showering in the streets of  spain scene looked amazing but the road  to achieving that product was a long and  frustrating one the money wouldn't fly  in the right direction because of the  wind and the weather was erratic  raining one minute and getting sunny  again shortly after the rain was what  really held them back  hundreds of extras were soaked without  anywhere to get shelter the paper bills  were wet and the set became ruined  needing to get the shot the team started  to improvise the paper money was dried  with giant fans the tools used to  collect the bills normally became dryers  for the ground  eventually they nailed it  the show can be awfully serious with  such high stakes but that didn't stop  the cast from having a lot of laughs on  set although not all of them wanted  people to know just how much they could  crack up  whether they were getting a bit over  dramatic with their line delivery  or interacting with the nature around  them when they were filming on location  the cast and crew enjoyed and made the  most out of the production  wearing glasses didn't help alvaro morte  at all while he was performing it was a  hindrance more than anything since the  actor actually has 20 20 vision he  wasn't the biggest fan of the prop  glasses but eventually got used to it  since it's such a signature part of the  look as for his nickname being the  professor and not a city the fact is he  actually does have a secret city  nickname vatican city reflecting just  how protected and mysterious his  character was  all that fake money flying around of  course couldn't be real for the shots  when we see the money stacked and  scattering the streets a million 50 euro  bills were printed using machines to  print newspapers and 6 000 golden bars  were created by the props department the  bars were actually made out of bronze  and the crew was even taught how to melt  it down into tiny nuggets but they left  the actual task to the professionals for  safety reasons of course  money heist didn't just gather loads of  fans many celebrities loved the show  including aladdin actor mina masood and  mindy kaling another famous fan went so  far as to ask to be part of it  soccer player neymar jr loved the series  so much he got in touch with the team  behind the show when the third season  came around the team found a role for  the football star he was the one who  played this brazilian monk  celestial  belachow has become such a powerful song  a group of immigrants rescued from a  boat saying it when they were safe and  on land while we heard it plenty in the  show it made more contributions than we  thought the season 3 opening includes a  shot of this doorway and above it we see  una matina misono alsato that line is  what starts off the song as well  the fact that the italian folk song  became an essential part of the series  was purely by chance the tune wound up  on a mix to inspire executive producer  and head writer javier gomez santander  while he was writing when thinking about  the right song to use in the celebratory  scenes santander heard it and knew it  was the right choice  it's hard to believe now but we could  have had a different actor portraying  the professor on screen javier gutierrez  was originally offered the complex part  but it conflicted with another project  the offer didn't go straight to morte  afterwards though the team saw him five  times over the course of two months  before finally making the offer as it  turns out we could have had alvaro morte  as the narrator of the series as well  ultimately though the team realized that  having the professor is the primary  voice we hear could come off as  narcissistic and affect how audiences  felt about the character tokyo seemed  like the perfect option to narrate  especially since onscreen the men  dominate  if you were trying to rob the bank of  spain the golden vault would actually  flood  loads of research was done to prepare  for the scene the team even brought a  marine engineer into the fold so they  could properly create the chamber it  turns out the thrill of seeing the  robberies in the series did inspire some  people to actually try their hand at  similar crimes some people who committed  these real-life crimes credited the show  as their source of inspiration going so  far as to wear the red jumpsuit and  salvador dali masks  yikes  alvaro morte and pedro alonso had  amazing chemistry on and off screen  together that relationship is all them  their characters berlin and the  professor weren't actually written to be  brothers it was the actors who thought  up the whole backstory including them  both being able to speak russian since  berlin went to russia with the professor  to get medical treatment years earlier  while some actors went through an  arduous audition process to win their  roles we're looking at you alvaro others  had straight offers for parts that were  literally written for them the character  albaflores plays nairobi didn't actually  exist in the first draft of the script  after revising the writing the team  wanted another woman playing a central  role and since alex pina had worked with  alba flores before he felt she would  make a perfect addition to the cast  thankfully flores accepted the offer and  brought nairobi to the screen for the  whole series  the unlikely success of money heist goes  to show just how great a series can be  if given the chance the production's  commitment to bringing authentic  storytelling to the screen including the  real stitches and hiring of specialists  to help bring accuracy to the bank vault  is impressive and a definite reason that  we love this series so much
 

